00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:50.920
so here's what you're looking for&nbsp;
number one you want a volatile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:54.600
solvent at the top of the ingredient&nbsp;
list volatile means that ingredient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:58.680
evaporates really easily and these are&nbsp;
the most common ones you'll see in makeup

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:02.480
the solvent itself isn't the bit that&nbsp;
makes it longwear but it's it's a sign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:06.760
that there are film forming polymers in&nbsp;
the product that will stick together after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:10.920
those solvents have evaporated off so the&nbsp;
solvent basically leaves and then the film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:15.720
forming polymers they can get together&nbsp;
and form a really nice long-lasting film

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:19.320
the second thing you're looking for is snug&nbsp;
packaging and again this just shows that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:22.720
there are volatile solvents in there there's&nbsp;
enough in there that they're looking for gas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:26.240
tight packaging so that stops these&nbsp;
volatile solvents from escaping and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:30.400
evaporating and making your product dry&nbsp;
out and shrivel and turn into like a lump

